---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CODE_FUNCTIONS, FUNCTIONS } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
const questionFile = FUNCTIONS.find((f) => f.notAFunction);
---
<Base title="Functions" description="The ten functions, simplest first.">
  <h1>The ten functions</h1>
  <p class="lede">ThinkThen gives your code ten functions that read text and answer a question about it. Each one does a job you already write in code: an if, a switch, a grep, a sort. The model gives three kinds of answer: yes or no, pick one, and place on a scale. The list runs simplest first.</p>

  <p>Diogo Almeida, TypeSafe's founder, maps the three to code you already write: "Choice maps into a switch statement on an enum. Nouls map to if statements. Scores map to sorting or thresholding."</p>

  <p>Noul, Choice, and Score are TypeSafe's names for yes or no, pick one, and place on a scale.</p>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Function</th><th>What it does</th><th>Kind of answer</th></tr>
    {CODE_FUNCTIONS.map((fn) => (
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`/functions/${fn.name}/`}><code>{fn.name}</code></a></td>
        <td>{fn.line}</td>
        <td>{fn.primitive}</td>
      </tr>
    ))}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="/functions/question-file/"><code>@question</code></a></td>
      <td>{questionFile.line}</td>
      <td>No answer</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p>A question file is a saved question. Every function accepts one, and it gives no answer of its own.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/surfaces/">Call it from your language</a> · <a href="/how-tos/">See the how-tos</a></p>
</Base>
